    "created_at": "2026-11-09T14:02:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T14:04:38Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure exactly what you are suggesting here. The bfcache relates to how `Document` objects get instantiated, it doesn't really relate to individual fetches.\n\nFrom what I saw, bfcache - in caching the entire Document - also caches the results of any fetch requests on that page, at least on Safari. In many web apps the results of fetch requests are directly used to render visible content, so cachign them on back navigation results in bugs. Is this just a Safari bug? I don't remember the exact behavior but I believe when a user back navigated, the fetch requests were replayed and the results were pulled from the bfcache.",
